#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("So, the Muslim Lantern clothing brand is finally here, alhamdulillah. And this is a clothing brand, guys. It is not a merch. And I'll tell you why I make this very, very clear and important distinction. I want you to understand the difference between a merch and a clothing brand. What a lot of people do, or let's say, maybe everyone, 90 to 95% or 99% of of the creators, what they do is they go to different websites, so many websites like this, Teespring and many other websites. What these websites do is that they design for you the clothing.", "You just give them a specific phrase or a word that you like, and then they print it on a t-shirt, and then they do everything. They do the the fulfilling, the buying, the selling. You have no clue about the item. You have no clue about the material being used. You don't know anything. And it's usually cheap material. And then you're just selling it to your audience. The website gets a cut, and you get a cut. So, it's something done with the purpose and the idea behind it of of course making money, and for people to support the person who's doing the content.", "But the idea is not to actually make a brand. A brand is where you actually make a a clothing from the start. And I'm going to talk to you guys about the process. There's so much effort and work that went into this. You guys know I haven't been doing it. I haven't ever done any sponsorship on my channel since I started it. Nothing. I haven't done a single sponsorship on my channel. And there's two reasons for that. First is I have to believe in the thing. I have to know who's doing it and why they're doing it and what their intentions are.", "But also it has to benefit the Muslim community as a whole. And that's why I usually avoided doing these type of things. Sponsorships on my channel. Cuz I need to do something that I believe in. Which is why I'm working on these projects. Doing something that I believe genuinely is going to have a positive impact on the Muslim community as a whole. So we've decided to make this clothing brand me and the team and I've been working on this for like nearly more than 2 years now. I've been traveling so much and people know I always talk about traveling and coming back.", "I don't remember how many times now I've been to Turkey and Istanbul. Because we have decided to make it in a Muslim country. So we chose to do it in Turkey for that reason because we wanted to make this in a Muslim country. And at the same time we wanted to do something that is quality. Everybody that you see that is doing these merch or selling clothing, they're manufacturing and things in China. That's why they will never tell you where their products are being made. We've actually put the effort, traveled ourselves. I've learned so much about textile.", "And I've been to factories. You'll see me like walking in factories, looking at the process of making of the caps and the hats. Looking at the process of making the clothing, dealing with manufacturers. Sometimes having very bad experiences and moving into other manufacturers. So we can in the end know what we're doing. So me learning about GSM, like the grams per square meter in the material, how heavy it is, how light it is, the woven techniques. The printing techniques, water based or 3D printing. For all of these things I've been spending my time learning about them.", "I've almost become a textile expert because of the amount of time that we put traveling, going to factories, looking at the manufacturing process, doing things over and over again because I have this issue of being OCD. So, I have to have everything done perfectly. Have to look perfect in every way, shape, or form, as much as possible. And And even my team is the same way. So, we've been struggling so much because of that. But, alhamdulillah, I'm very happy about the result. So, you see me wearing the pray, believe, achieve in the Palestine kind of color, which is really, really beautiful.", "It's one of my favorites. And actually on the uh right-hand side, you will see that you have the Muslim Lantern logo. Actually, a lot of people don't know this, but the logo is actually the word Muslim in Arabic calligraphy. So, I'm sure you guys are going to like this a lot. You will see the quality when you buy it, inshallah. It's very comfortable. The coloring, most importantly, doesn't fade away. You know, I was talking about these major brands of these believer major brands. You buy the item, and it's so expensive. You wash it once or twice, the color fades away, it ruptures, you throw it away.", "And this has happened to me so many times. And I know many Muslims have these experiences. Why? Because these brands are out there to make money. What they want is to make money. That's it. So, they go on mass producing in China. If we wanted to do this, I would have released this like maybe 2 years ago. I wouldn't have spent 2 years going into factories myself, traveling all over Turkey, visiting different manufacturers, looking at the process, redoing things over over again, changing different materials. If your goal is just to make money, it's very easy for you to do.", "But, our goal was the quality and something that truly represents the Muslims. Even though it will not be as cheap as something that you get from China, but if I buy this t-shirt and I keep it, it will remain with me. Color will remain. It will stay with me for a very long time, and it will remain as a quality clothing. Then go buying something very cheap, throwing it away after a couple of wears. So, our focus was the quality, something that represents the Muslims, something that we can actually be proud of wearing, and it can represent our identity.", "Pray, believe, achieve, things that represents us as Muslims. Not things that are benefiting the non-Muslims and being used to support you know, the killing of our brothers and sisters. So, what makes it unique is the quality, the comfort, and in the Muslim identity in the clothing. Inshallah, I'm going to put a lot of effort into this. I've already put a lot of effort and time and resources. I'm not going to talk about the details, but if you guys see the process I'm talking about from beginning to end, not only the traveling that I've been talking to you about, but everything.", "So, company to fulfill the the orders and take care of them. We have a worldwide shipping, wherever you are, inshallah, you can get the clothing, you can buy it, you can have it delivered to you. We've had a specific modeling company and a studio rented so we can model the clothing so things can be as professional as possible. Every item has been modeled, we edited it, we had it looked at. You can look at the website, you can look at how professional the website is. Everything is there, the details of the clothing, the GSM used, where it was manufactured, the sizing, everything you probably can think about, you will see on the website.", "By looking at the website, you'll see how much effort and time we've put into this. Here is some of the products you guys have seen. This is the one that I'm wearing, which is one of my favorites because of the Palestine theme, the pray, believe, achieve. We have it in multiple colors. We have it in white, we have it in black. Then we also have the true monotheist design. We also have it in different colors, white and we have it in black. And then you have the classic tee. So, the classic tee has a Muslim logo, and it also has white color and black color.", "So, if you are one of the simplistic people that would just like the classic tee, you can get that one. If you like the designs, which inshallah we'll have a lot more in the future. Then you also have the hoodie, which is also one of my favorites. We have two versions of it. You have the kangaroo hoodie, and you have the zipper hoodie. And I'm telling you, you will see the attention to detail that you guys will know we're not just doing things for the sake of them. So, if you look at the hoodie even, you look at the uh metal zipper, you will see the logo is there on the metal zipper.", "Every detail of these items, we've spent so much time and so many samples. If you look at the design on the kangaroo and the design on the hood, this design says in Arabic calligraphy al-ghina ghina al-qalb. So, richness is the richness of the heart, which is a hadith of the prophet alayhi salat wa salam. So, you can see it in Arabic calligraphy there. Then we have the hats. Let me actually show them to you here before I show them to you on the website. So, I have some of them here. So, we have the cotton hat.", "So, this is just a classic hat. This is all cotton. And we have the nylon hat. So, it's the same hat, but it's nylon. The material is nylon. It's really nice, actually. I like this one a lot. Then we have the half and half, which is half cotton and half mesh, right? For people who like that. And by the way, you'll see the interior design has the logo here. You'll see the word Muslim in inside and the design of the hat. And I have this one, which I actually would probably say is my favorite. It's the full mesh one.", "And the reason it's my favorite is because I can travel with it and because it's mesh material, it doesn't kind of change structure because I travel so much. So, I can show them to you here also on the website. You can see them. We have the nylon hat, we have the cotton, and we have the half and half, and we have the mesh as well. If you guys inshallah want to test it out, want to try it, and want to support the channel, want to support the vision. The most important thing is supporting the vision of us having actually a Muslim brand because like I said, I'm going to put my effort into this inshallah.", "It's not just something I'm releasing. The purpose behind it is not making money. The purpose behind it is to do something that is quality that is going to remain with you. So, like I said, even if you look at it and you're like, \"That's uh more expensive than what I can buy in this cheap store.\" Yeah. If you go and buy in that cheap store, they're selling you something that is made in China. We are selling you something that is truly quality. Something that we've tested ourselves and we've tried ourselves. Something that you'd be comfortable wearing, happy wearing.", "It's not only supporting the creator. It's not about making money, but it's about supporting the vision of being a Muslim yourself. So, we have a very limited launch, of course, because this is the initial launch. So, I would recommend you guys get one before it's gone. So, inshallah, you can go on the website, muslimlantern.com. You can go over there. We have also a limited time discount for the initial launch. So, inshallah, you're able to get it before the discount is over. It's going to be there for a while, inshallah, not not for too long, though.", "So, I'd recommend you get it as quickly as you can. And inshallah, like I said, there will be a lot more designs. There will be a lot more items and accessories and things that are going to come. And inshallah, this is going to be a brand that represents us as Muslims. And if you get it, inshallah, and you wear it, post it on social media. You can tag me. You can send it to me. You can DM it to me. You can let me know if you have any concerns, if you have any issues, what you really think of it.", "I'm going to be really happy to get the feedback from everyone. And inshallah, you guys are going to like it. And like I said, stay tuned because there's another massive project that is coming very soon, inshallah, in the next couple of weeks. Uh we're also going to release. May Allah Azza wa Jal bless you all. If you got any questions, specific questions, leave them for me in the comments. I'll try and respond to them. Uh inshallah, I usually don't respond to the comments, but I will do in this video to do with the branding and anything you guys have to say about it, inshallah.", "So, may Allah Azza wa Jal bless you all. And I hope you like it. And please let me know what you guys think of it. And get yours today, inshallah, before it's gone. Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi",))
